Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:03:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] TIP 759 (7/7): argument expansion {*} in expressions

{*} before an argument of a function or an element of a list expands
the value as a list, as in a command: max({*}$L, 0), (0, {*}$L).
{*} is recognized only when immediately followed by the start of an
operand, so {*} eq "*" keeps its meaning. Elsewhere it is an error.

Compiled with expandStart / expandStkTop / invokeExpanded.

Tests: tests/exprExpand.test. Documentation: expr.n.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MrNWAEyXLqekovNBvbMZ4z
