 .QW "cmd a b {[c]} d {$e} f {g h}" .
+.TP 5
+\fBArgument expansion in an expression.\fR
+.VS TIP759
+If an argument of a function, or an element of a list, starts with the
+string
+.QW {*}
+immediately followed by the start of an operand, then the leading
+.QW {*}
+is removed and the rest of the operand is evaluated as any other
+operand. Its value is then parsed as a list, as in a command, and each
+of its elements becomes a separate argument of the function, or a
+separate element of the list. For instance, if the value of \fBL\fR is
+\fB3 1 2\fR, then
+.QW "max({*}$L, 0)"
+is equivalent to
+.QW "max(3, 1, 2, 0)" .
+Anywhere else in an expression, this prefix is an error; but
+.QW {*}
+followed by white space or by an operator, as in
+.QW "{*} eq \N'34'*\N'34'" ,
+is the braced string \fB*\fR (rule [6]).
+.VE TIP759
+.RE
 .IP "[6] \fBBraces.\fR"
 If the first character of a word, or of an operand of an expression,
 is an open brace
